WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.245 --> 00:00:02.036
-Hi. I'm Antonio Brown,

00:00:02.036 --> 00:00:03.863
and you're watching
"Simms &amp; 'Let-go'"

00:00:07.053 --> 00:00:09.155
-[ chuckles ]
What up, "Let-go"?

00:00:09.155 --> 00:00:12.225
-Antonio, if you do that again,
you're in big-time trouble, pal!

00:00:12.234 --> 00:00:14.447
It is Lefkoe, it is Simms.

00:00:14.453 --> 00:00:17.325
That's the way
it should be said.

00:00:17.325 --> 00:00:18.426
This is Chris Simms.

00:00:18.442 --> 00:00:19.786
He is a football savant.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.122
You know his dad.
Seven years in the NFL.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.525
-Eight years,
you freakin' idiot.

00:00:23.525 --> 00:00:26.162
-But he's got a beautiful mind,
watches more film than anybody.

00:00:26.172 --> 00:00:28.962
-Right.
And this is Adam Lefkoe,

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:32.474
the host, my work wife,
and the biggest mouth I know,

00:00:32.474 --> 00:00:34.142
and he doesn't even --
not that good of a friend.

00:00:34.142 --> 00:00:35.661
He didn't know I played
eight years in the NFL.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.307
Thanks, friend.
-Doesn't matter.

00:00:37.307 --> 00:00:39.054
We have a lot of friends we're
gonna introduce you to today.

00:00:39.054 --> 00:00:40.289
First, young guy.

00:00:40.636 --> 00:00:43.885
-This is Sam Darnold!
What?!

00:00:43.911 --> 00:00:45.734
And then we go from the
East Coast to the West Coast,

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.049
and we got Marcus Peters
coming on, Lefkoe.

00:00:49.225 --> 00:00:50.894
-Hanging out with some LA Rams.

00:00:50.913 --> 00:00:52.715
What are you best
at gambling at?

00:00:53.432 --> 00:00:55.411
-At shooting dice.
-And we sat down with a guy

00:00:55.411 --> 00:00:58.615
that took Chris' dad's job,
Tony Romo.

00:00:58.621 --> 00:01:00.757
I actually think Sam Darnold,

00:01:00.757 --> 00:01:00.790
I actually think Sam Darnold,
He's the best quarterback

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:01.557
He's the best quarterback

00:01:01.557 --> 00:01:02.692
to come out in a while, period.

00:01:02.925 --> 00:01:05.662
-All that is coming up
on "Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:01:05.662 --> 00:01:07.397
But first, Chris,
a little segment for them.

00:01:08.631 --> 00:01:11.934
-It is time
-For Whoa, Big Headline

00:01:12.201 --> 00:01:13.836
We had a big headline
over the weekend.

00:01:13.836 --> 00:01:15.204
-What?
-We were going nuts.

00:01:15.204 --> 00:01:16.506
One of the best
defensive players

00:01:16.506 --> 00:01:17.840
in the NFL, Khalil Mack...

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.942
-Yes.
-...traded to the Bears,

00:01:19.942 --> 00:01:21.844
and Chicago is pumped,
and they should be.

00:01:21.844 --> 00:01:23.546
-Holy cow.
-Boom!

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:26.849
Khalil Mack turns the Bears
into a playoff team.

00:01:26.849 --> 00:01:29.719
We had them at, like,
the 9-7 wildcard fight.

00:01:29.719 --> 00:01:31.721
-Right, the fringe team.
-Are they in?

00:01:31.721 --> 00:01:33.156
-I mean, they're scary.

00:01:33.156 --> 00:01:34.857
-I want a bold prediction.
-They're scary.

00:01:34.857 --> 00:01:36.859
Let me just say this --
Monsters of the Midway.

00:01:36.859 --> 00:01:40.063
Khalil Mack, Roquan Smith,
Leonard Floyd, Akiem Hicks --

00:01:40.063 --> 00:01:42.899
the Bears defense will be
one of the best in football.

00:01:42.899 --> 00:01:45.234
-And we love Vic Fangio.
-We love Vic Fangio.

00:01:45.268 --> 00:01:47.003
-And now he has
so many chess pieces.

00:01:47.003 --> 00:01:48.538
-Yes, he does.
I look at Khalil Mack

00:01:48.538 --> 00:01:50.773
like he used Aldon Smith
a few years back for the 49ers.

00:01:50.773 --> 00:01:52.809
Outside linebacker,
defensive end

00:01:52.809 --> 00:01:54.844
coming off the edge.
They're gonna create havoc.

00:01:54.844 --> 00:01:56.312
Poor Aaron Rodgers.

00:01:56.345 --> 00:01:58.147
Watch out for
the Bears' front seven.

00:01:58.147 --> 00:01:59.982
-There's a sad side.
-Yeah.

00:02:00.016 --> 00:02:02.151
-The Raiders.
I love Raiders fans.

00:02:02.151 --> 00:02:03.553
-We love the Raiders.

00:02:03.586 --> 00:02:05.555
-Trading Khalil Mack
was the right move

00:02:05.555 --> 00:02:08.491
for the Raiders --
the Las Vegas Raiders.

00:02:08.491 --> 00:02:10.860
These Oakland people
are getting screwed.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.562
I'm just gonna
put it out there -- this stinks.

00:02:12.562 --> 00:02:13.963
-He's the best player
on the team.

00:02:13.963 --> 00:02:15.098
It's not even close.

00:02:15.098 --> 00:02:16.866
He was the defensive MVP
two years ago.

00:02:16.866 --> 00:02:19.102
I don't get it.
It obviously was a money thing.

00:02:19.102 --> 00:02:20.837
-Of course.
-But the Raiders defense,

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.271
its lack of talent.

00:02:22.271 --> 00:02:24.173
-It was already bad.
-It was below average,

00:02:24.173 --> 00:02:25.875
and now I don't know
what it is going to be.

00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:27.577
-All right, last one.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.577 --> 00:02:31.180
-Davis Webb, who was the star of
the off-season, shocking move.

00:02:31.214 --> 00:02:32.882
-He's so amazing
in the meeting room.

00:02:32.882 --> 00:02:35.785
-He's got binders,
he has playlists for Eli,

00:02:35.785 --> 00:02:37.920
and he's brought back
his cowboy boots.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.456
-His arm is so strong...
-How strong is it?

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:41.891
-...it was almost too strong.

00:02:41.891 --> 00:02:43.559
-He literally said that.

00:02:43.559 --> 00:02:44.927
Here's a thing, though.

00:02:44.927 --> 00:02:46.696
They passed on a quarterback
in the draft,

00:02:46.696 --> 00:02:49.499
and Davis Webb's like,
"I'm the heir apparent to Eli."

00:02:49.532 --> 00:02:51.000
-Right.
-Does this make you question

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.535
the Saquon draft with all these

00:02:52.535 --> 00:02:54.036
rookie quarterbacks
looking good?

00:02:54.036 --> 00:02:55.738
-No. First of all,
Davis Webb, like,

00:02:55.738 --> 00:02:58.541
self-appointed him
the heir apparent to Eli,

00:02:58.541 --> 00:02:59.776
so pump the brakes there.

00:02:59.809 --> 00:03:01.344
Giant fans want Eli.

00:03:01.344 --> 00:03:03.746
That's all they cried for
the last year and a half.

00:03:03.746 --> 00:03:05.515
I'll tell you what I'm worried
about with the Giants.

00:03:05.515 --> 00:03:09.352
If Eli gets hurt, their backup
quarterbacks are not very good.

00:03:09.352 --> 00:03:11.788
This just in -- doo-doodle-doo,
doo-doodle-doo!

00:03:11.788 --> 00:03:13.189
-That's breaking news.
-Thank you.

00:03:13.189 --> 00:03:15.725
-So, we do know that Webb
is going to the Jets,

00:03:15.792 --> 00:03:18.127
but the future, as you mention,
Sam Darnold.

00:03:18.127 --> 00:03:21.998
We got Sam Darnold, rented a
little car, just us three guys.

00:03:21.998 --> 00:03:23.466
-Little fun.
-Wanted to show him

00:03:23.466 --> 00:03:25.468
New York City,
but we did invite some friends.

00:03:29.772 --> 00:03:34.510
-J-E-T-S --
Jets, Jets, Jets!

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:37.113
[ cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.885 --> 00:03:45.221
-Are we ready to give Sam
a tour of the city?

00:03:45.221 --> 00:03:47.023
-Yeah!
-Let's go!

00:03:47.023 --> 00:03:49.425
-Wave to your admirers.
They're out there.

00:03:49.458 --> 00:03:51.561
Win over New York.

00:03:51.561 --> 00:03:53.329
-Let's go, Giants!

00:03:53.362 --> 00:03:54.964
-Yeah.
-All righty.

00:03:54.964 --> 00:03:56.666
-You're gonna have to hear that
today. I'll shut them up.

00:03:56.666 --> 00:03:58.301
Did you have to do
any rookie hazing yet?

00:03:58.301 --> 00:04:00.436
Have you had to take everybody
to dinner or anything?

00:04:00.436 --> 00:04:01.904
-I had to sing.
I had to sing, yeah.

00:04:01.904 --> 00:04:04.006
-What'd you go with?
-"Thousand Miles."

00:04:04.006 --> 00:04:05.875
-"Thousand Miles."
- by Vanessa Carlton.

00:04:05.908 --> 00:04:07.476
-Yeah.
-  Da-na-na, na-na-na-na.  

00:04:07.476 --> 00:04:08.711
-I just want to admit something.
-Yeah.

00:04:08.711 --> 00:04:10.880
-I'm a little upset that you get
to sit next to Sam.

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.782
-When you were briefed
about this, they were like,

00:04:12.782 --> 00:04:14.517
"Yeah, you're gonna sit..."

00:04:14.517 --> 00:04:16.052
-You're from Philadelphia.
-You're right.

00:04:16.052 --> 00:04:17.386
I don't know this area too well.

00:04:17.386 --> 00:04:19.255
-'Cause when me and Chris
are talking,

00:04:19.255 --> 00:04:22.024
you're not even really
part of it, you know?

00:04:22.992 --> 00:04:25.895
-To really know New York,
there are a certain group

00:04:25.895 --> 00:04:28.030
